  "lineage": "Gugak gwanhyeonak is the large conducted orchestra of Korean traditional instruments, arranged in sections like a Western orchestra and playing newly composed works (changjak gugak) and arrangements. The Seoul Metropolitan Traditional Music Orchestra was the first, followed by the KBS Korean Traditional Music Orchestra and the National Orchestra of Korea, which use enlarged and reformed instruments such as the 25-string gayageum.",
